# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Coverage and test-report output. Measured in CI and uploaded as an artifact; a local run leaves
# these behind and none of them belong in a commit.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
pytest-report.xml
# The visual smoke reel (M2) - a rendered video, produced on demand and by CI.
#
# `smoke_source.*` and `synth_bed_*` are intermediates `scripts/smoke_reel.py` writes into the
# working directory when it synthesises a source rather than being given `--source`. Listed here
# because the script is now run by CI, so they appear in a clean checkout.
smoke_reel.mp4
smoke_source.*
synth_bed_*
mutation-report.txt
# Hypothesis example database / cache written by the test runner
.hypothesis/

# Environment
.env

# Storage artefacts (keep the directory structure, ignore contents)
storage/uploads/*
storage/temp/*
storage/clips/*
# Durable per-clip engine artifacts persisted through the storage backend
# (e.g. retained stem WAVs under storage/engines/<job>/<clip>/<engine>/).
storage/engines/*
# T8: cached transcripts are derived data, regenerated on demand.
storage/transcripts/*
!storage/transcripts/.gitkeep
storage/*.db
storage/*.db-wal
storage/*.db-shm
# Runtime state written by the app (user-tunable config + saved profiles)
storage/runtime_config.json
storage/profiles.json
!storage/**/.gitkeep

# Emoji assets ARE committed (A7). This used to ignore them with the comment "downloaded
# at build time", and no build step did that - so assets/emoji was empty and the overlay
# had nothing to composite. scripts/fetch_emoji.py is that build step, and its output is
# tracked so a render never depends on a CDN.
#
# The *alternative* artwork sets (A13) are not committed: three sets over 326 glyphs would
# triple the ~7 MB the assets cost, to ship two looks most installs never select. They are
# per-machine caches, populated by `scripts/fetch_emoji.py --style <name>`.
assets/emoji-*/

# Node / frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Publisher bridge (Node @whop/sdk) — install at build time, commit the lockfile
publisher_bridge/node_modules/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp

# S1 evaluation harness: labels are committed (they are the benchmark), footage and cached
# transcripts are not. A transcript cache is derived data keyed on file size and mtime, and
# the footage is the user's own media - neither belongs in the repository.
eval/cache/
eval/media/
eval/*.json
!eval/labels/*.json


# Cached static ffmpeg build fetched by scripts/setup_dev_env.sh, so a re-run after a
# recycled environment is a copy rather than a 42 MB download.
.devtools/



# SARIF written by the CodeQL workflow. It lands in the workspace (rather than the action's default
# location outside it) so the run can archive it and gate on it; that also puts it in reach of
# `git add`, which is the only reason this line is needed.
sarif-results/



# The VMAF-capable ffmpeg CI fetches for the fidelity gate (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
# Cached between runs by actions/cache, and downloadable locally the same way, so it is never
# something to commit — it is a 114 MB third-party binary.
.ffmpeg-vmaf/
